# wishbusterz-rider — optional API keys.
#
# Everything here is OPTIONAL. The six offline domains and the `live` domain need
# no keys at all. Copy this file only if you want measured PageSpeed scores or
# the Google registration checks:
#
#   cp .env.example .env      # .env is gitignored — never commit real keys
#
# The tool reads plain environment variables; it does not load .env itself.
# Export them in your shell, or use your runner's secret store (in GitHub
# Actions, repository secrets — see .github/workflows/audit.yml).

# ─── Measured PageSpeed / Core Web Vitals (the `lighthouse` domain) ────────────
#
# A free key, ~2 minutes, no billing: open the Google Cloud console, enable the
# "PageSpeed Insights API", then create an API key.
#   https://developers.google.com/speed/docs/insights/v5/get-started
#
# Without it the lighthouse domain ⏭ skips and everything else still runs.
# PSI needs a PUBLICLY REACHABLE url — it cannot see localhost.
PAGESPEED_API_KEY=

# ─── Advanced: is the site registered and measured? (the `google` domain) ──────
#
# Only worth setting up if you own the Search Console / Analytics properties for
# the domain you audit. Needs a Google Cloud service account with the Search
# Console API, Site Verification API, and Analytics Admin API enabled, that
# service account granted read access to your GA account, and added as a user on
# the Search Console property. Budget ~20 minutes the first time.
#
# Supply the downloaded key as raw JSON (or base64 of it):
# GOOGLE_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_JSON=
#
# …or point at the key file instead (Google's own convention):
# GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS=/path/to/service-account.json

# The Zaraz leg of the `google` domain checks that your GA4 measurement ID is
# actually wired into Cloudflare Zaraz. Needs a Cloudflare API token with
# "Zaraz: Read" and "Zone: Read". Skips independently of the two above.
# CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN=
